WEBVTT

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:04.700
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.260
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:15.530
This is the story of
their lives and adventures.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.380
Go!

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:26.850
Go!

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:30.760
Wake up, Go. It’s morning!

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:34.030
Dad?

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:37.540
Good morning.

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:40.010
Come on, it’s the start of a new day.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:44.440
A-Aaaaaaaagh!

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:46.780
M-M-M-M-M-Mom!

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:49.060
Th-This is crazy, Dad has...

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:51.780
What? Why are you shouting?

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:53.900
Is something wrong, Go?

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:56.020
No, uh...

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:57.120
Then never mind that...

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:00.810
Here, watch your
little brother for me, okay?

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:13.550
That... was a dream?

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:16.590
That was a shock...

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:03.430
Wh-What’s wrong?

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:08.040
It’s a Pokémon!
Where’d that come from?

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:12.900
Sarunori. Chimp Pokémon.
Grass type.

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:15.000
It attacks with rapid beats of its stick.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:19.490
As it strikes with amazing speed,
it gets more and more pumped.

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:24.620
Huh. Sarunori’s a
Pokémon from Galar, isn’t it?

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:27.830
Satoshi, have I turned
into a Gorillander?

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:29.260
A Gorillander?

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:32.650
The final evolution of Sarunori.

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:34.610
I think you need to wake up.

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:37.440
So, where’d that Sarunori
come from?

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.050
It was here when I woke up.

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:39.780
Huh?

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:41.670
That’s awesome!

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:44.730
Oh, Pikachu...

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:46.990
Are you trying to copy Sarunori?

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:53.710
Actually, if I think about it,
this is really lucky, isn’t it?

00:03:57.990 --> 00:03:59.860
Monster Ball...

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:01.220
Go.

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:03.430
Don’t be a thief!

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:04.790
Huh?!

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:05.710
Then...

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:08.510
Sarunori already
has a trainer?!

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:10.480
Guess so...

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:14.490
I wonder who it belongs to...?

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:15.550
Yeah.

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:19.590
It woke up.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:27.410
Ow! Ow, ow!

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:27.910
Hey!

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:29.830
Ah, ow!

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:30.330
Hey!

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:38.540
Barrierd!

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:00.310
It got serious.

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:03.840
Looks like it’s stubborn
on top of being mischievous.

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:10.810
Huh?

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.160
What happened?

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:16.990
Oh, I see.

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:20.500
It’s just like Satoshi.
It completely shuts down when it’s hungry.

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:22.510
Let’s go and have breakfast!

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:29.000
Must’ve been really hungry...

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:32.980
Yeah! I’d even run out on meals
to have breakfast!

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:34.980
I meant the Sarunori,
not you...

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:48.490
Hey, stop that!

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:48.980
Hey!

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:50.120
Ow...

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:51.950
Stop!

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:55.250
I said stop!

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:56.390
Huh?

00:05:57.620 --> 00:05:59.400
Where’d it go?

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:02.130
Hey! Sarunori!

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:04.630
Ahh! Messon!

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:10.010
What were you doing in there?

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:12.890
Stop!

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:16.080
Okay, I’ll be off.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.100
See you later.

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:24.730
What?! What is this?!

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:26.240
What?

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:28.070
No!

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:29.570
Stop it, Sarunori! Hey!

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:36.830
What is all this?! Geez...

00:06:37.340 --> 00:06:39.030
Isn’t that a Sarunori?

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:40.350
What is it doing here?

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:42.960
I’ll explain later.
Just help me catch it!

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:46.710
No!

00:07:00.410 --> 00:07:04.020
I see. So you woke up with it
clinging to your arm.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:08.150
And it’s not wild,
but already someone’s partner.

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:10.830
You never know what life’s
gonna throw at you, huh?

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:14.250
Oh! Maybe it’s Gänger
playing tricks?

00:07:15.970 --> 00:07:17.360
Sounds like a no.

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:19.690
S-Sorry for suspecting you...

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:27.130
Anyway, we can’t just
let it be, yeah?

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:28.330
Yeah.

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:32.210
If it has a partner,
they might be worried sick about it.

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:32.890
Yeah.

00:07:33.670 --> 00:07:37.810
It looks like there aren’t any online reports
of lost Sarunori, at least.

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:39.750
What should we do, Go?

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:44.210
That’s it! Wanpachi!

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:48.810
If we use Wanpachi’s nose
to trace Sarunori’s footsteps,

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:50.890
maybe we can find out
where it came from!

00:07:50.890 --> 00:07:52.530
Oh, that’s a nice idea!

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:57.180
Yes. If it works, you may be able to
reunite it with its partner.

00:07:57.180 --> 00:07:59.290
Okay! Wanpachi,
we’re counting on you!

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:05.780
First, we have to find out
how it got into our room.

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:08.970
Wanpachi, this is
the scent to track, got it?

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:14.460
That way?

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:15.720
Looking good.

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:24.730
The door’s open!

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:32.610
So this is where it got in...

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:34.520
So it climbed up here?

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:37.670
What is it, Wanpachi?

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:44.200
Huh? Down?

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:47.080
Back to square one, huh...?

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:56.180
Is this the place, Wanpachi?

00:08:59.110 --> 00:09:00.320
It just leapt in!

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:04.360
That might mean...
Its partner lives here!

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:08.030
Excuse me!

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:11.680
We’d like to ask you
about a Sarunori!

00:09:18.830 --> 00:09:19.910
Stop!

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:35.420
Hey, hold on!

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:37.870
The weather’s so nice today...

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:47.060
Stop it, Garagara!

00:09:49.990 --> 00:09:51.950
Stop, Sarunori!

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:03.660
It stopped moving again.

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:10.550
Sheesh... You’re really
digging in, huh?

00:10:10.550 --> 00:10:14.100
Well, I’d even run out on meals
to have lunch.

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:16.010
I meant the Sarunori, not you!

00:10:19.350 --> 00:10:20.090
Sarunori?

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:37.930
Sarunori did that?

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:40.450
It has the power
to revitalize flowers!

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:43.340
It’s kinder than I thought.

00:10:43.340 --> 00:10:46.660
Well, it could just be playing around.

00:10:47.890 --> 00:10:51.130
Ow, ow... Stop that...

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:03.370
What is it?

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:07.040
Is this the end of the scent trail?

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:08.520
Here, though?

00:11:12.130 --> 00:11:13.910
Let’s ask inside the shop.

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:18.990
In that case, the surveillance cameras
might have caught something.

00:11:19.460 --> 00:11:21.640
Could we take a look?

00:11:21.640 --> 00:11:23.120
Go ahead.

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:31.790
That’s...

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:33.540
Team Rocket’s...

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:49.560
No way...

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:54.340
Sarunori...

00:11:54.340 --> 00:11:56.440
...belongs to Team Rocket?!

00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:02.340
Pocket Monsters!

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:19.960
Sarunori... Are you really
a Team Rocket Pokémon?

00:12:23.830 --> 00:12:25.950
Don’t worry, I’m not mad!

00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:26.930
It’s just...

00:12:28.940 --> 00:12:29.660
What’s this?!

00:12:29.660 --> 00:12:31.810
If you ask us about “this” or “that”...

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:34.690
We’ll answer out of
sympathy for the world!

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:37.990
To protect the world from devastation.

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:40.780
To preserve world peace.

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:43.780
Championing the evils
of truth and love.

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:46.990
We’re the lovely, charming villains.

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:48.400
Musashi!

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:49.460
Kojiro!

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:52.910
The Team Rocket duo
soars through the galaxy!

00:12:52.910 --> 00:12:56.210
Like a white hole,
a white tomorrow awaits us!

00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:58.500
Just kidding, meow!

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:05.450
Team Rocket! You jerks again!

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:07.050
Our target, the Pikachu...

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:09.570
...and Sarunori,
the rare Pokémon from Galar...

00:13:09.570 --> 00:13:11.180
It’s a double catch, meow!

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:12.690
We won’t let you!

00:13:12.690 --> 00:13:14.020
Kamonegi!
Crossroad Kill!

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:19.190
Brutal Swing!

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:25.080
Ow, ow...

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:25.880
...Huh?

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:27.030
In that case...

00:13:27.420 --> 00:13:29.630
Vending, come on!

00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:36.620
And here it is.

00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:41.730
Rocket Vending Secret!

00:13:41.730 --> 00:13:43.210
What’re we gonna get?

00:13:45.230 --> 00:13:47.640
Huh? Wait, only one?!

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:51.640
Go for it,
super strong Pokémon!

00:13:56.810 --> 00:13:58.310
What’s going on?!

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:02.460
The Chimp Pokémon,
Sarunori?

00:14:02.460 --> 00:14:05.550
The Chimp Pokémon...
Sarunori?

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:08.910
Oh no, no way, no way...

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:13.410
What, so like, that Sarunori was supposed to
be in this Monster Ball,

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:16.260
and so if I said
“Return, Sarunori,”

00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:19.080
it’d go “Clin-clin-cling and click,”
back into here...?

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:20.500
That’s completely ridicul—

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:21.810
It’s true!

00:14:21.810 --> 00:14:22.710
What?!

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:23.920
Sarunori!

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:26.200
Let’s retreat for now,
and try again later!

00:14:26.200 --> 00:14:27.670
Nyanparari!

00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:30.740
Sarunori!

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:48.280
That was a real surprise, meow.

00:14:56.890 --> 00:14:58.510
That’s Morpeko’s box!

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:02.380
Saved it...

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:03.210
Hey!

00:15:03.650 --> 00:15:04.750
Saved it.

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:07.400
Hey! What’re you doing?!

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:12.300
Y-You’ve got it wrong, meow!

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:13.880
It was <i>that one,</i> not us...

00:15:13.880 --> 00:15:15.390
You can’t do that, Sarunori!

00:15:32.790 --> 00:15:34.160
Go!

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:36.980
Sorry. What is it?

00:15:36.980 --> 00:15:38.470
Can I turn off the light?

00:15:38.470 --> 00:15:40.160
Oh. Yeah.

00:15:50.350 --> 00:15:52.920
Were you thinking about Sarunori?

00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:55.360
Huh? Yeah...

00:15:55.360 --> 00:15:57.430
My arm just feels empty...

00:15:58.400 --> 00:16:00.610
It was a funny Pokémon.

00:16:01.280 --> 00:16:02.020
Yeah.

00:16:02.910 --> 00:16:05.690
Who could’ve thought
it was Team Rocket’s...

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:09.570
Do you think it’s
having fun right now?

00:16:14.050 --> 00:16:15.720
I hope so...

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:42.640
Go!

00:16:43.030 --> 00:16:45.900
Where are you going?
Aren’t you having breakfast?

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:49.900
I thought I should give Sarunori
its stick back, at least.

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:53.880
But if we don’t know
where Team Rocket are...

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:56.870
Right. That’s why I’m gonna
find them somehow.

00:16:58.040 --> 00:17:00.750
Okay. Then I’ll help, too!

00:17:01.970 --> 00:17:03.060
But Satoshi,

00:17:03.060 --> 00:17:05.270
Didn't you say you’d
run out on meals to have breakfast?

00:17:07.590 --> 00:17:08.960
I brought it with me!

00:17:11.320 --> 00:17:13.300
It’s gone, it’s gone, it’s gone!

00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:15.430
Sarunori’s gone!

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:19.290
Not good, that was a Pokémon
dispatched by HQ!

00:17:19.290 --> 00:17:22.310
They won’t accept it
just disappearing, meow!

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:26.770
We’ll leave no patch of grass unturned,
if we have to!

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:28.620
It’s a “Grass”-type, get it?

00:17:28.620 --> 00:17:30.190
Turf pun, meow.

00:17:31.560 --> 00:17:34.670
Team Rocket shows up
whenever we don’t want them,

00:17:34.670 --> 00:17:37.730
but now we’re looking for them,
they’re nowhere to be found...

00:17:39.480 --> 00:17:41.050
The park from yesterday.

00:17:43.570 --> 00:17:45.000
Huh? Are they here?

00:17:56.210 --> 00:17:57.340
Go...

00:18:04.770 --> 00:18:06.250
Sarunori!

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:12.010
I’ve missed you, Sarunori!

00:18:13.470 --> 00:18:15.900
I’m really happy for you,
Go, Sarunori.

00:18:18.120 --> 00:18:20.340
This is important to you, yeah?

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:23.410
Thank you for the delivery!

00:18:24.590 --> 00:18:25.660
Team Rocket!

00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:28.190
And if you were going to say
“You jerks again”...

00:18:28.190 --> 00:18:30.440
That’s our line, meow!

00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:34.590
You wanna try to steal our Pokémon
not just once, but twice?!

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:36.920
Now, come on back, Sarunori!

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:40.500
What? You don’t want to?

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:42.690
Whether you want to or not,

00:18:42.690 --> 00:18:44.980
as long as we have this Monster Ball...

00:18:46.650 --> 00:18:49.270
You belong to Team Rocket!

00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:52.020
We’ll send you back to HQ
and have you re-educated...

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:53.900
...into a Pokémon that
champions evil!

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:55.320
What?!

00:18:55.320 --> 00:18:57.740
Hey! Huh? Hey!

00:18:57.740 --> 00:19:00.570
Stop it!
Can’t you see it’s refusing?

00:19:00.570 --> 00:19:02.660
Shut it! Stay out of the way!

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:04.240
Pikachu!

00:19:16.990 --> 00:19:20.560
What?! You want Brat Boy Mk. II
to catch you?!

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:23.550
Is that true, Sarunori?

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:26.930
What’d you translate that for?!

00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:29.770
Meow! I was just lying, meow!

00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:32.600
Okay! Let’s go, Sarunori!

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:34.350
My turn first!

00:19:34.350 --> 00:19:36.620
Monster Ball, Go!

00:19:53.260 --> 00:19:56.920
Sarunori’s data will be
added to the index!

00:19:56.920 --> 00:19:59.270
All right!

00:20:01.070 --> 00:20:02.720
Come on out, Sarunori!

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:08.570
What do we do, Musashi?

00:20:08.570 --> 00:20:10.480
We’ll just have to go back to the basics.

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:15.730
Catching Pikachu with this
Ultra Super Bespoke Throw Net DX, meow!

00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:18.360
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!

00:20:26.720 --> 00:20:29.350
<i>What an awful feeling!</i>

00:20:42.570 --> 00:20:47.310
And so, Sarunori officially
became one of my Pokémon.

00:20:50.950 --> 00:20:52.480
It’s so cute!

00:20:52.950 --> 00:20:55.440
It’s already getting along
with Pikachu and Wanpachi.

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:57.940
I wonder if it’ll make friends
with Eevee.

00:21:02.950 --> 00:21:05.930
Oh! Sarunori,
are you apologizing?

00:21:05.930 --> 00:21:07.580
Saying “Sorry about yesterday.”

00:21:07.580 --> 00:21:09.950
You hear that, Eevee?

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:18.590
Okay! Looks like it should be able to fit in
with the other Pokémon, too.

00:21:27.840 --> 00:21:29.260
You can’t do that, Sarunori!

00:21:29.940 --> 00:21:32.600
Hey, stop!

00:21:33.490 --> 00:21:38.280
With the addition of Sarunori,
Sakuragi Park is all the livelier.

00:21:38.280 --> 00:21:41.970
How will Sarunori
end up developing?

00:21:41.970 --> 00:21:43.420
Stay tuned!

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:51.720
Mew!

00:21:51.720 --> 00:21:52.470
Warrgle!

00:21:52.470 --> 00:21:53.260
Runpappa!

00:21:53.260 --> 00:21:54.030
Pawou!

00:21:54.030 --> 00:21:54.770
Ulgamoth!

00:21:54.770 --> 00:21:55.560
Strike!

00:21:55.560 --> 00:21:56.360
Cresselia!

00:21:56.360 --> 00:21:57.070
Amakaji!

00:21:57.070 --> 00:21:57.880
Jirachi!

00:21:57.880 --> 00:21:58.680
Chobomaki!

00:21:58.680 --> 00:21:59.450
Kibago!

00:21:59.450 --> 00:22:00.220
Gonbe!

00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:01.000
Bayleaf!

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:02.500
Freezer!

00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:03.690
Zacian!

00:22:19.770 --> 00:22:20.540
Mew!

00:22:20.540 --> 00:22:21.370
Wooper!

00:22:21.370 --> 00:22:22.090
Pachirisu!

